**Mechanism found.** The research lane's valid q-bar windows must sit inside one session day, so a 12-hour window can only end after 06:00 ET, inside the London and New York high-volatility hours, while the denominator averages 5-minute variance over the whole day including quiet Asian hours. Volatility seasonality alone pushes VR above 1 as q grows. The Lo-MacKinlay z tests against VR=1, which is the wrong null under that window selection. Once returns are standardized by time-of-day, every window and nearly every year shows VR below 1 at all horizons, and the size matches the lag-1 autocorrelation alone. Gold M5 is a random walk plus a 5-minute reversal, with no multi-hour structure in either window. Cycle19's conclusion that the recent edge is not explained by intraday trendiness therefore stands and is stronger.

