| Mechanism | Pre-entry atr/risk correlates with path volatility at 0.64 and reproduces the gap alone at −0.241 (t −2.36). Path volatility normalized by pre-entry ATR gives −0.034 (t −0.33). The effect is entry geometry, not path shape. |

**The "quiet trades run" reading (W2)** passes my pre-fixed descriptive rule (day-cluster t 2.20, block bootstrap CI excludes zero) but is BUY-only (+0.237 vs SELL +0.029) and tail-driven, so it reads as gold's 2021-26 uptrend on long-remaining BUY positions, the same drift cycle18 already described.

**Most severe refutation of cycle23's reading.** The residual is the interaction "high atr/risk and still near zero after 24 bars", present only in 2021-23, absent in all trades at entry and outside the stalled bin. The same atr/risk variable surfaced post-hoc in a different path cell on 11-04 and 11-05 and was broken then. This is its second out-of-sample-only appearance.

**Counter-evidence to my own verdict, recorded.** The linear day-clustered effect reaches t −3.40, the narrower stall bin gives t −2.99, and the k-sweep is negative across nearly every k out-of-sample while flat in-sample. Those are correlated views of one cell and do not survive the family-wise test, but they are not nothing. A forward pre-registration would need about four years of new data for the observed effect size, so a 250-day design cannot pass.

